# Architecture

## Stack
Next.js App Router, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS, next-intl, Framer Motion, React Three Fiber.

## Directory Layout
```
src/
  app/           # Routes, layouts, metadata
  components/    # ui/, layout/, sections/, animations/, 3d/
  features/      # Domain-specific modules
  lib/           # Utilities, cn(), constants
  services/      # Data access, CMS/DAM adapters
  hooks/         # Custom React hooks
  providers/     # Context providers
  types/         # Shared TypeScript types
  config/        # App configuration
  data/          # Mock/static data (temporary)
  i18n/          # Locale config and messages
```

## Principles
- Server Components by default; `"use client"` only for interactivity, hooks, browser APIs, 3D, animations.
- Colocate feature logic in `features/`; keep `components/` presentational.
- All external data flows through `services/` adapters — never import CMS SDKs in components.
- Use `@/` import alias consistently.
- One `h1` per page; semantic HTML throughout.

## Routing
- Locale prefix: `/[locale]/...` via next-intl middleware.
- Route groups for layout variants: `(marketing)`, `(admin)` (future).

## Env
- Secrets in `.env.local` only; document in `.env.example`.
- Access env via `src/config/env.ts` with validation.
